version 0.14.0
module debug-header

# Case 10 of the ten (AGENTS.md §10, docs/backlog.md F12): the three ways a pin can be unconnected.
#
#   1. `no_connect` — a fact of the device: pin 7 (key) and pin 8 (unused) are dead pins of this
#      connector. They stay out of every net; the component file owns those no-connect pin facts.
#   2. intentionally open — pin 9 (GNDDetect) is a live pin this board does not use. It stays out
#      of every net and is marked `no_connect` in this module's interface, preserving the deliberate
#      choice rather than treating it as an accidental omission.
#   3. connected — everything else, including the pull-up that keeps the target out of reset when
#      no probe is attached.
#
# SWDIO / SWCLK / SWO each reach only one pin here (the target end is off-board), so they are
# exposed as ports: a net that ends at a port is not single-member (teda.md §11.4).
instances
  J1  IDty8s4q  hdr-2x5-127
  R1  IDv66dfw  res-10k-0402

nets
  GND:    J1.3  J1.5
  NRST:   J1.10  R1.1
  SWCLK:  J1.4
  SWDIO:  J1.2
  SWO:    J1.6
  VTREF:  J1.1  R1.2

ports
  GND        GND
  GNDDetect  no_connect
  NRST       NRST
  SWCLK      SWCLK
  SWDIO      SWDIO
  SWO        SWO
  VTREF      VTREF
